Abstract: This document describes the general architecture of the FAIR Data Train (FDT): the roles and the components of an FDT ecosystem, how the components interact — trains travel to Data Stations and run there under agreements negotiated on arrival, behind policy checkpoints that decide what may leave — and the open standards each part is built on. It is the entry point to the FDT specifications; the protocol between a Data Station and a Train Handler is specified in the companion FDT Visit Protocol.
